The patch updates the check in `l2tp_udp_recv_core` to ensure that at least 14 bytes can be pulled from the skb, which matches the maximum size of the L2TPv2 header. This change prevents the function from attempting to read beyond the bounds of the skb, thus eliminating the risk of memory corruption or crashes when handling L2TP packets with optional fields.


